doc_id: surrealdb-connection-pooling-patterns
title: SurrealDB Connection Pooling Patterns
project: ai-workflow
version_hint: "2024-2025"
kind: surrealdb_pooling_standards
description: SurrealDB-specific patterns for connection pool implementation, configuration, lifecycle management, and schema initialization using SurrealDBPool.
scope: Covers SurrealDB pool design, asyncio.Queue-based pooling, pool configuration (size, timeouts), connection lifecycle (startup, auth, schema init, shutdown), schema initialization patterns, and SurrealDB-specific testing. Generic pooling concepts are in python/connection-pooling-patterns.toon.
out_of_scope[3]:
  - Generic pooling fundamentals (see python/connection-pooling-patterns.toon).
  - FastAPI lifespan integration (see fastapi/connection-pooling-patterns.toon).
  - Repository query patterns (see surrealdb/repository-patterns.toon).
primary_runtime_references[2]:
  - path: app/infrastructure/surrealdb/pool.py
    role: SurrealDBPool implementation with asyncio.Queue-based pooling.
  - path: app/core/settings.py
    role: Pool configuration fields (surrealdb_pool_size, acquire_timeout).
related_pattern_docs[5]:
  - python/connection-pooling-patterns.toon
  - fastapi/connection-pooling-patterns.toon
  - surrealdb/repository-patterns.toon
  - python/factory-patterns.toon
  - python/settings-patterns.toon
sections[5]:
  - id: surrealdb-connection-pool
    index: 1
    title: SurrealDB connection pool
    category: standard
    summary: Design and usage patterns for SurrealDBPool.
    sample_code:
      description: Typical SurrealDBPool usage pattern for executing a query.
      imports[2]: app.infrastructure.surrealdb.pool.SurrealDBPool,typing.Any
      code: |
        from typing import Any
        from app.infrastructure.surrealdb.pool import SurrealDBPool
        async def run_query(pool: SurrealDBPool, sql: str, params: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> Any:
            async with pool.acquire() as conn:
                result = await conn.query(sql, params or {})
                return result
    items[5]:
      - id: surreal.pool-async-queue
        type: rule
        text: SurrealDBPool maintains multiple WebSocket connections to SurrealDB in an asyncio.Queue, creating them up front during initialization.
      - id: surreal.pool-config-size
        type: rule
        text: Control pool size via Settings.surrealdb_pool_size so concurrency can be tuned per environment without code changes.
      - id: surreal.pre-authenticated
        type: note
        text: During initialization, each SurrealDB connection is authenticated and pointed at the configured namespace and database so queries do not repeat this work.
      - id: surreal.acquire-context-manager
        type: pattern
        text: Use SurrealDBPool.acquire() as an async context manager that enforces an acquire timeout and automatically returns connections to the pool when the context exits.
      - id: surreal.exception-safety
        type: note
        text: The async with pool.acquire() pattern ensures connections are returned even if downstream queries raise exceptions.
  - id: surrealdb-pool-configuration
    index: 2
    title: SurrealDB pool configuration
    category: standard
    summary: Recommended configuration options for SurrealDBPool.
    items[4]:
      - id: surreal.config.pool-size
        type: rule
        text: Start with a conservative surrealdb_pool_size (for example 5) and increase only when metrics show SurrealDB is the bottleneck and the server can handle more concurrent connections.
      - id: surreal.config.acquire-timeout
        type: rule
        text: Configure an acquire_timeout of several seconds on SurrealDBPool and enforce it via asyncio.wait_for() so callers fail fast rather than hanging indefinitely.
      - id: surreal.config.env-specific
        type: note
        text: Treat pool size and acquire timeout as environment-specific knobs, using smaller values for local development and tuned values for staging and production.
      - id: surreal.config-focus
        type: note
        text: Keep pool-related settings focused on connection counts and wait times rather than unrelated SurrealDB configuration.
  - id: surrealdb-connection-lifecycle
    index: 3
    title: SurrealDB connection lifecycle
    category: standard
    summary: Startup, schema initialization, and shutdown behavior for the SurrealDB pool.
    sample_code:
      description: Factory function that creates and initializes a SurrealDB pool.
      imports[2]: app.core.settings.Settings,app.infrastructure.surrealdb.pool.SurrealDBPool
      code: |
        from app.core.settings import Settings
        from app.infrastructure.surrealdb.pool import SurrealDBPool
        async def create_surrealdb_pool(settings: Settings) -> SurrealDBPool:
            """Factory that builds and initializes a SurrealDB pool from settings."""
            pool = SurrealDBPool(
                dsn=settings.surrealdb_url,
                namespace=settings.surrealdb_namespace,
                database=settings.surrealdb_database,
                user=settings.surrealdb_user,
                password=settings.surrealdb_pass,
                size=settings.surrealdb_pool_size,
                embedding_dimension=settings.embedding_dimension,
            )
            await pool.init()
            try:
                await pool.initialize_schema()
            except Exception:
                await pool.close()
                raise
            return pool
    items[5]:
      - id: surreal.lifecycle.startup
        type: pattern
        text: Call create_surrealdb_pool(settings) during startup to build a SurrealDBPool, initialize connections, and make it available for dependency injection.
      - id: surreal.lifecycle.auth
        type: note
        text: During initialization, the pool authenticates each connection and selects the configured namespace and database so subsequent queries can assume a ready session.
      - id: surreal.lifecycle.schema-init
        type: rule
        text: After creating the pool, call pool.initialize_schema() to set up tables, relationships, and vector indexes required by the application.
      - id: surreal.lifecycle.fail-fast
        type: rule
        text: If schema initialization fails, close the pool and propagate the error so the application fails fast instead of running with partial schema state.
      - id: surreal.lifecycle.shutdown
        type: rule
        text: During shutdown, call surrealdb_pool.close() and log any failures without preventing process termination.
  - id: schema-initialization
    index: 4
    title: Schema initialization
    category: standard
    summary: How schema setup ties into connection pooling.
    items[4]:
      - id: schema.initialize-in-pool
        type: rule
        text: Run SurrealDB schema initialization inside SurrealDBPool.initialize_schema() so it executes immediately after pool creation.
      - id: schema.versioning
        type: note
        text: Track schema versions using a schema_versions table or similar mechanism to manage migrations safely; see _get_current_schema_version() and _write_schema_version() in pool.py.
      - id: schema.factory-calls-init
        type: pattern
        text: Ensure create_surrealdb_pool() calls initialize_schema() and closes the pool if initialization fails.
      - id: schema.failure-fatal
        type: rule
        text: Treat schema initialization failures as fatal; the app must not start with an inconsistent or partially-applied schema.
  - id: surrealdb-testing
    index: 5
    title: Testing SurrealDB pools
    category: testing
    summary: Strategies for testing code that uses SurrealDB pools.
    sample_code:
      description: Monkeypatching create_surrealdb_pool for tests.
      language: python
      code: |
        import pytest
        from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock
        @pytest.fixture
        def mock_surrealdb_pool():
            """Create a mock SurrealDBPool for unit tests."""
            pool = MagicMock()
            pool.acquire = AsyncMock()
            pool.close = AsyncMock()
            pool.initialize_schema = AsyncMock()
            return pool
        @pytest.fixture
        def patch_create_surrealdb_pool(monkeypatch, mock_surrealdb_pool):
            """Patch create_surrealdb_pool to return a mock pool."""
            async def mock_factory(settings):
                return mock_surrealdb_pool
            monkeypatch.setattr(
                "app.infrastructure.surrealdb.pool.create_surrealdb_pool",
                mock_factory,
            )
            return mock_surrealdb_pool
    items[5]:
      - id: test.monkeypatch-factory
        type: pattern
        text: Monkeypatch create_surrealdb_pool() to return mock pools in tests that only care about validation or error behavior.
      - id: test.mock-acquire
        type: rule
        text: Configure mock pools with mock.acquire() returning a mock connection that captures query arguments for assertion.
      - id: test.integration-namespace
        type: pattern
        text: For integration tests, use a separate SurrealDB namespace/database (for example test_namespace) to isolate test data from development data.
      - id: test.cleanup
        type: rule
        text: Clean up test data between test runs by deleting records or resetting the test database; avoid side effects between tests.
      - id: test.docker-compose
        type: note
        text: Integration tests can use docker-compose to spin up a SurrealDB instance for the test suite; see tests/conftest.py for fixture examples.
